"Stack moves the real app into its own folder: it disappears from Applications, Launchpad and Spotlight, and you open it from Stack. Nothing inside the app is changed and it keeps its settings. If it's open, it quits and reopens. macOS may ask for your password. Updates from the App Store may no longer find it, and its own “open at login” may stop working (put it in an “open on click” group instead). You can put it back in Applications at any time." = "Stack moves the real app into its own folder: it disappears from Applications, Launchpad and Spotlight, and you open it from Stack. Nothing inside the app is changed and it keeps its settings. If it's open, it quits and reopens. macOS may ask for your password. Updates from the App Store may no longer find it, and its own “open at login” may stop working (put it in an “open on click” group instead). You can put it back in Applications at any time.";
